codex
I found a concrete new blocker: the fence catches every exception from an anchor `head_at` and continues. A transient failure at the abandoned coordinate therefore produces ADVANCED, journals the abandoned head, and the next open is UNCHANGED—the original self-erasing loop. I reproduced that exact three-state sequence with a real ledger wrapped only to fail the anchor lookup. I’ll finish the claimed suite/count/doc checks, but this already prevents convergence.
